# Migration files can contain function bodies whose source was captured
# byte-for-byte from the live database (see supabase/migrations/20260827120000_baseline_from_live.sql).
# Some of those bodies have Windows-style line endings (\r\n) embedded
# literally inside them, because that's what's actually stored in the
# database. Without this rule, git's automatic line-ending conversion
# (the same one that prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on Windows)
# would silently strip those out on commit, reintroducing drift between
# this repo and the live database every time the file is touched.
supabase/migrations/*.sql -text
